  "response": "I’m using the `crimes-codebase-risk` workflow to ground the refactor proposal in the reported finding, then I’ll inspect the four matching JSX subtrees so the component API reflects the real differences.\n\nThe duplicated shape is the form action footer—not the invoice fields: a right-aligned wrapper containing the Cancel link and the submit button. The only current variation is the submit label (“Create Invoice” vs “Edit Invoice”), which makes a small slot-based component a better fit than abstracting the whole form.\n\nFinding `crime_00064` identifies the repeated form-action footer across four invoice forms.\n\nProposed component: `InvoiceFormActions`\n\n```tsx\ntype InvoiceFormActionsProps = {\n  cancelHref: string;\n  cancelLabel?: React.ReactNode;\n  children: React.ReactNode; // primary/submit-action slot\n};\n```\n\n```tsx\nexport function InvoiceFormActions({\n  cancelHref,\n  cancelLabel = \"Cancel\",\n  children,\n}: InvoiceFormActionsProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n      <Link href={cancelHref} className=\"...\">\n        {cancelLabel}\n      </Link>\n      {children}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nUsage:\n\n```tsx\n<InvoiceFormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\">\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Create Invoice</Button>\n</InvoiceFormActions>\n```\n\nThe `children` slot deliberately accepts the complete primary action rather than a `mode: \"create\" | \"edit\"` prop. That preserves support for specialized submit controls, pending states, or additional accessibility behavior without adding conditionals to the shared component.\n\nFiles to modify:\n\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx`\n\nIf these examples are intended to share source, add:\n\n- `dashboard/shared/ui/invoices/invoice-form-actions.tsx`\n\nIf `starter-example` and `final-example` must remain independently runnable tutorial snapshots, put the same conceptual component in each app instead:\n\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n\nThat second placement still eliminates create/edit drift within each application without coupling the two examples’ build boundaries.",
